Package: netpair
Version: 0.1.5-1
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Nicolas Cisco <nicolas@nckweb.com.ar>
Installed-Size: 7868
Depends: passt, iproute2
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/nickcis/netpair
Description: isolated network namespace pairs for processes
 netpair runs process pairs in isolated network namespaces with Internet
 access, local port relay, and native SSH port forwarding.
 .
 Each pair uses pasta from the passt package for networking. iproute2
 provides ss(8) used by netpair connect for automatic port discovery.
 .
 On Ubuntu 24.04 there is an AppArmor profile for pasta
 (/etc/apparmor.d/usr.bin.pasta); pasta requires it when unprivileged
 user namespaces are restricted (the default there). Run 'netpair doctor'
 to verify the environment.
